  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center">
    
  <html:span style="font-size: 2em">Dyck derivation trees</html:span>

    <html:p><html:em>Generated from a real</html:em> <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathtt {DyckAST}]]></fr:tex> <html:em>term, not hand-drawn.</html:em></html:p>
    <html:p><html:span style="font-size: 0.75em"><fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathtt {mt} : \mathtt {DyckAST}]]></fr:tex> \quad 
       <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathtt {bal} : \mathtt {DyckAST} \to  \mathtt {DyckAST} \to  \mathtt {DyckAST}]]></fr:tex>
       \quad  term: <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathtt {bal}\;\mathtt {mt}\;\lparen \mathtt {bal}\;\lparen 
       \mathtt {bal}\;\mathtt {mt}\;\mathtt {mt}\rparen \;\mathtt {mt}\rparen ]]></fr:tex></html:span></html:p>
  </html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center"><html:p><html:strong>As an inference-rule derivation</html:strong></html:p> 
  <html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">(grows bottom-up)</html:span>
</html:div>

  
  <html:div class="dtree" data-mode="inf" data-loop="true">
    <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-spec"><![CDATA[{"rule":"bal","concl":"()(()) : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"bal","concl":"(()) : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"bal","concl":"() : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]}]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]}]}]}]]></html:script>
  </html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="text-align: center"><html:p><html:strong>The same term as a parse tree</html:strong></html:p> 
  <html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">(grows top-down)</html:span>
</html:div>

  
  <html:div class="dtree" data-mode="parse" data-loop="true">
    <html:script type="application/json" class="dt-spec"><![CDATA[{"rule":"bal","concl":"()(()) : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"bal","concl":"(()) : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"bal","concl":"() : Dyck","kids":[{"tok":"("},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]}]},{"tok":")"},{"rule":"nil","concl":"ε : Dyck","kids":[]}]}]}]]></html:script>
  </html:div>

</html:section>

  <html:section>
  
  <html:div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center">
    <html:p><html:span style="font-size: 1.4em">No fake inductive type.</html:span></html:p>
    <html:p>The JSON above is the output of <html:code>toSpec : DyckAST -&gt; String</html:code> ---
       a fold over the <html:em>real</html:em> inductive parse-tree type in
       <html:code><![CDATA[ Examples.Benchmark.Dyck]]></html:code>. A parse produces a
       <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathtt {DyckAST}]]></fr:tex> via <html:code>abstractify</html:code>; <html:code>toSpec</html:code> folds it to this
       spec; the renderer is two more folds (parse view / inference view).</html:p>
    <html:p><html:span style="font-size: 0.75em">Regenerate: <html:code>C-c C-n</html:code> on <html:code>exampleJSON</html:code> in
       <html:code><![CDATA[ Examples.Generic.DyckSpec]]></html:code>.</html:span></html:p>
  </html:div>

